---
title: Configure Environment Variables
description: Set up the backend .env file with your Vonage Application ID and private key so the server can authenticate with the Video API.
---

# Configure Environment Variables

The backend reads its configuration from a file called `backend/.env`. A template with all available variables is provided at `backend/.env.example`.

The setup script already copied that template for you. Open `backend/.env` in the editor now — it looks like this:

```ini
# backend/.env

VIDEO_SERVICE_PROVIDER='vonage'
VONAGE_APP_ID=''
VONAGE_PRIVATE_KEY=''

SESSION_KEY_SECRET=''
```

You need to fill in three values.

---

## VONAGE_APP_ID

Replace the empty string with the Application ID you copied from the Vonage dashboard in the previous step:

```ini
VONAGE_APP_ID='xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx'
```

---

## VONAGE_PRIVATE_KEY

Open the `private.key` file you downloaded from the dashboard in a text editor. Copy the **entire contents** of the file — including the `-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----` header and `-----END PRIVATE KEY-----` footer — and paste it as the value, keeping the surrounding single quotes:

```ini
VONAGE_PRIVATE_KEY='-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----
MIIEvQIBADANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAASCBKcwggSjAgEAAoIBAQC7...
-----END PRIVATE KEY-----
'
```

> **Note:** The closing `'` must appear on its own line, after the key footer.

---

## SESSION_KEY_SECRET

This secret is used to sign the JWT cookies that track meeting-room sessions. Set it to any long, random string — for example:

```ini
SESSION_KEY_SECRET='change-me-to-a-long-random-secret-string'
```

> **Security tip:** In production, generate this value with a cryptographically secure random generator, for example:
> ```bash
> node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
> ```

---

## Complete example

After filling in all three values, your `backend/.env` should look similar to:

```ini
VIDEO_SERVICE_PROVIDER='vonage'
VONAGE_APP_ID='12345678-abcd-1234-abcd-123456789abc'
VONAGE_PRIVATE_KEY='-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----
MIIEvQIBADANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAASCBKcwggSjAgEAAoIBAQC7...
-----END PRIVATE KEY-----
'

SESSION_KEY_SECRET='a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2'
```

> **Do not commit** `backend/.env` to source control — it is already listed in `.gitignore`.

---

The backend is now fully configured. In the next step you will install the project dependencies and start the application.
